    {
      "id": "arunachal-pradesh",
      "name": "Arunachal Pradesh",
      "geography": {
        "capital": "Itanagar",
        "key_cities": []
      },
      "facts": [
        "**Jewellery**: made of brass, bone, ivory, silver, and gold are made by many tribes of Arunachal Pradesh. The Monpas are known traditional silversmiths. Brass is skilfully shaped into ornaments, dishes, sacred bells and smoking pipes. The Khamtis work mainly in gold, iron, silver and ivory. The Gallong women wear ear-plugs and earrings. Plugs are generally of leaf, wood or bamboo, while the rings are heavy and coiled and made of iron. The rings are and specially used by the Gallong women. Beads of various colours and sizes, blue feathered wings of birds and green wings of beetles are also used as embellishment."
      ],
