        "handicrafts": [
          {
            "id": "plhwmc50o",
            "title": "Arunachal Pradesh - Handicrafts",
            "name": "Arunachal Pradesh - Handicrafts",
            "desc": "Arunachal Pradesh is a land of beautiful handicrafts where people have a tradition of artistic craftsmanship. A wide variety of crafts such as weaving, painting, pottery, basketry, woodcarving etc. are found among the people here.",
            "img": "https://indianetzone.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/baad3-bamboo-handicrafts-of-arunachal-pradesh.jpg",
            "historical_significance": "",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "n0vw18wry",
            "title": "Bamboo Craft",
            "name": "Bamboo Craft",
            "desc": "The craftsmen of Arunachal Pradesh make various cane and bamboo articles for domestic requirements. Bamboo and cane are found in abundance in this region due to the heavy rainfall and temperate climate. The tribal population uses these materials almost exclusively for constructing their dwellings, utensils, furniture, and even weapons such as bows and arrows, spears, armor, and implements like dibbles, hunting and fishing traps. Bamboo and cane are also transformed into colorful basket mats, cane belts, attractive smoking pipes, combs, and a variety of household tools and",
            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/bamboo-craft.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "0m8cplmmy",
            "title": "Arunachal Pradesh - Handicrafts - Carpet",
            "name": "Arunachal Pradesh - Handicrafts - Carpet",
            "desc": "One of the important creative activity in the district of Tawang, is the weaving of carpets. A speciality of the Monpas, the Buddhist community, is that it is done mainly by women. The weaving is done with exotic designs of dragons, geometric and floral patterns.",
            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/carpet.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "l4at6w9dr",
            "title": "Arunachal Pradesh- Handicrafts- Handlooms",
            "name": "Arunachal Pradesh- Handicrafts- Handlooms",
            "desc": "Weaving is an important household industry involving the women of Arunachal Pradesh. The actual weaving is done with a bamboo tube and using cotton and wool. Bark fibres extracted from trees like udal, pudu and grasscloth is also used. The designs are essentially geometric varying from formal arrangement to lines and bands. The colors that are generally used in the weaves are black, yellow, dark blue, green and scarlet - all put together in the most fascinating combinations. There is an abundant use of natural dyes in the weaving though a lot of synthetic dyes are now used. The Tibetan and Bhutanese influence is evident in the Monpa loom on which the Monpa women weave with cotton, wool and bark fibre. They are well known for their fine and colourful coats, shawls, sashes, carpets, bags and tapes (for tieing around hats). The Apatanis are traditionally the most advanced weavers of the state producing excellent ceremonial coats and shawls, and embroidered cotton cloth.Many tribes such as the Nishis, Hill Miris, Akas, Bugums and Mijis depend on the Apatanis for their supply of cloth. Singpho weaving is famous for its artistic patterns. Similarly, the Tangas are reputed for their spun-dyed clothes out of which they make handbags,",
            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/weaving.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "fuz7sqt5p",
            "title": "Arunachal Pradesh- Handicrafts- Woodcarving",
            "name": "Arunachal Pradesh- Handicrafts- Woodcarving",
            "desc": "Woodcarving has a long tradition among the Monpas, Khamtis, Wanchos, Phom and Konyak tribes. The main center for woodcarving and woodcraft in the state is the Wancho area of Tirap district. The Wancho woodcarvings have three functions. The first is the one connected with headhunting; the second with the decoration of the Morungs or men\u0092s communal houses; and the third with the funerary images of different animals. The Wancho wood carver has a deep sense of proportion. In carving of the human figure, special attention is paid to the head. The features are carved in low relief and are fairly realistic. The tribes like Monpas, Sherdukpens, and Bugums create a variety of coloured masks. The masks are made of a single block of wood hollowed inside and holes are usually but not always made for eyes and mouths. Masks are only worn by boys and men. Women never wear",
            "img": "/state-images/Arunachal_Pradesh/woodcarving.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "d52j5bldp",
            "title": "Arunachal Pradesh- Handicrafts- Pottery",
            "name": "Arunachal Pradesh- Handicrafts- Pottery",
            "desc": "Women of the Dafla clan are accomplished potters. Finished pots are not polished or burnished but are carefully kept in the shade for drying. When completely dry, they are put in a fire out-side the house. There are no kilns or pot-ovens. Pottery is used primarily for making cooking utensils.",
            "img": "https://abirpothi.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Courtesy-Indian-Retailer-1024x602.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "806ba700",
            "title": "Handwoven wool shawls",
            "name": "Handwoven wool shawls",
            "desc": "Handwoven wool shawls",
            "img": "https://shop.gaatha.com/image/catalog/Vankar-Babubhai-Ladhubhai/12_12_2019/woolen-shawl.jpg"
          },
          {
            "id": "081f16fe",
            "title": "yak wool textiles",
            "name": "yak wool textiles",
            "desc": "yak wool textiles",
            "img": "http://www.primitivetribalcraft.com/cdn/shop/files/hand_woven_yak_wool_shawl003.jpg?v=1746425774"
          },
          {
