        "handicrafts": [
          {
            "id": "75fas6nwo",
            "title": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts - Handloom",
            "name": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts - Handloom",
            "desc": "One of the finest silk made in India is made in Assam and it is available in a wide range. Among the silk, the Muga is the most elegant which are of naturally rich golden colour. The skill to weave is seen as one of the eligibility criteria of a young girl for a marriage.",
            "img": "/state-images/Assam/muga_silk1.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "wle89h4cn",
            "title": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts - Terracotta",
            "name": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts - Terracotta",
            "desc": "The practice of making terracottas has been flourishing throughout in Assam since ages and this craftsmanship has transmitted from one to the other. Some of the common figures start from the figures of Gods to mythological characters. The two potter communities namely the Kumhars and the Hiras are living in Assam. The Kumhars use the wheel to produce their pots but the Hiras do not use the wheel. Some of the products are earthen pot and pitchers, plates, incense stick holders and earthen lamps.",
            "img": "/state-images/Assam/terracotta.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "iuwd13u9f",
            "title": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts - Metal Work",
            "name": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts - Metal Work",
            "desc": "The workmanship of this craft can be found in the traditional utensils and fancy articles. Fancy articles like xorai and bota used for offering betel-nut and paan have been popular and used till now. Hajo and Sarthebari, two townships near Guwahati have the whole population working in metal. The most used metals are the bell-metal and brass.",
            "img": "/state-images/Assam/180px-Assam_Xorai.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "wnmwyvx87",
            "title": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts -Toys",
            "name": "Assam \u0096 Handicrafts -Toys",
            "desc": "Clay toys, pith, wooden and bamboo toys, cloth toys, cloth-and-mud toys are produced in Assam. Human figures like dolls and brides and grooms and a variety of animal forms are the most common forms of toys. The clay toys are in the form of gods, goddesses and other mythological figures. Clays of Pith or Indian cork made in the Goalpara region have been popular for centuries.",
            "img": "/state-images/Assam/toys.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "3e3e967a",
