    {
      "id": "goa",
      "name": "Goa",
      "geography": {
        "capital": "Panaji",
        "key_cities": []
      },
      "facts": [
        "**Crochet and Embroidery**: It is due to the arrival of the nuns and missionaries from Portugal that the craft of crochet and embroidery found roots in Goa. In due course of time it developed fast and found its way in almost every house of Goa. At the time of marriage, a few pieces of embroidered linen and crochet are given to the bride as part of her trousseau. It is customery in Goa with both, Christians and Hindus to display before the guests the crochet and embroidery items the bride has brought with her at the time of marriage. This perhaps is to demostrate the skills of the bride in crochet and embroidery work. The craft of crochet and embroidery is passed on from one generation to another, with a variation in quality and design."
      ],
