          {
            "id": "aku5y0eex",
            "title": "Artefacts & site of Rakhigarhi",
            "name": "Artefacts & site of Rakhigarhi",
            "desc": "Prehistoric 5000 BCE In Haryana, pre Harrapan and Harrapan sites have been found. The major sites from where evidences of civilization are visible are Rakhigarhi, Banawali, Kunal, Agroha, Mittathal and Naurangabad. These sites have traces of paved roads, drainage system, a large rainwater collection and storage system, terracotta brick and statue production, and skilled metal working (in both bronze and precious metals) has been uncovered. Bangles made from terracotta and conch shells, have also been found. Marks of ploughed and cultivated fields, tools for ploughing, stone and",
            "img": "/state-images/Haryana/rakhigariwheel.webp",
            "historical_significance": "",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "h44yt7qn7",
            "title": "Pottery",
            "name": "Pottery",
            "desc": "Potters and pottery making is an integral part of rural India and Haryana is no exception Potters are found in almost all the villages where they make utensils, decorative pieces and toys. Seasonal festivals are the times when the potters hundreds of toys like miniature cows, horses, people and houses.",
            "img": "/state-images/Haryana/Ha_008.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "ihxvnk649",
            "title": "Textiles-Weaving",
            "name": "Textiles-Weaving",
            "desc": "Haryana is very famous for its woven work, like shawls, durries and lungis. The durries from Haryana are embellished with spectacular geometric designs. The durries made with white triangles often set against a blue background is a popular pattern. Panipat is the centre for durrie making.",
            "img": "/state-images/Haryana/hand-knitted-durries.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "05pd5sj4k",
            "title": "Artisans demonstrating at Surajkund mela",
            "name": "Artisans demonstrating at Surajkund mela",
            "desc": "Surajkund is famous for the crafts fair held in February every year. The fair brings together crafts persons including potters, embroiderers, weavers, wood carvers, metal workers, stone smiths, painters etc. from all over India. For entertainment there are performances by folk dancers, musicians, acrobats and magicians.",
            "img": "/state-images/Haryana/surajkund-mela.webp",
