            }
          ],
          "classical": [
            {
              "id": "4016a302",
              "name": "Kathak",
              "desc": "Kathak, which means storytelling, is a dance form from northern India, particularly rooted in the regions of Uttar Pradesh and Rajasthan. Kathak evolved as a form of storytelling through expressive gestures, intricate footwork and graceful movements. Dancers captivate audiences with swift  spins, rhythmic foot stamping, delicate hand gestures, and nuanced facial expressions to bring stories to life. Among the many gharanas of kathak the Lucknow, Jaipur, Banaras, Raigarh styles are particularly renowned though several other gharanas have also shaped and enriched the form. They stand tall in a posture called sama sthana, with feet together or in a slight v-shape. The costumes are usually long, flowing dresses like anarkalis or lehengas, with dupattas made from fabrics typical to northern India.",
              "img": "/downloaded_images/bee506e3593ea6b855c0022b40f02ce3.webp",
              "images": [
                "/downloaded_images/bee506e3593ea6b855c0022b40f02ce3.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/5a150e70cfa38dd7498a92fd0a1019f3.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/a19084d341dfef7a763da70e4fcc603f.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/2636020d4d5de081dbe9eda9da1f20ae.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/976dfdfe8aa8730ef8ff91ffbe166320.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/b0ee140aa884f57b650e22effb06ff75.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/af8dea6226f5c07e34d50a8921f8144f.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/4e64a7fc6c98cf58b189970fae42ba5a.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/9f480a2611146cfcf620c59ff9b66657.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/2291696457377f2b7420cb44e50f528c.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/cad70737d69965ca209d0b253abe765f.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/4b4d111c31b026014f95ff56d5c8a009.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/2dca87af229c0b7e21fe55b32aad75f9.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/2b9227a7f6053b409579116e6ce48d07.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/de39b3d8bb4e7f54942143f72f2ae425.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/e367cb0aad717cf51f016ca120f012d3.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/ff477550a5042d958623e86e010271ae.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/3cf11936ca8ab47a523ea13eb43ded06.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/c7beb7c1637030d915091aa843654b88.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/088960e318eb07a21d4f7a2e5628b10e.webp"
              ],
              "artists": "1.Sitara Devi \n\n2.Shambhu Maharaj - Scion of the Lucknow Gharana of Kathak (Padma Shri in 1958)\n(Ref: NCERT Textbook gekr1, Ch. 13) \n3.Birju Maharaj - (Ref: NCERT Textbook gekr1, Ch. 13) \nScion of the Lucknow Gharana of Kathak, Shambhu Maharaj belongs to a family of traditional Kathak dancers. His forefathers were gurus and dancers at the court of Nawab Wajid Ali Shah of Awadh. His father was the famous Kalka Prasad and uncle Binda Deen, who consolidated the Lucknow Gharana of Kathak. Trained under his uncle Binda Deen. Later, he established a post-independence with his elder brother Acchan Maharaj repetorrie of dance. He made his debut in Lucknow in 1926 at the All India Music Conference after which he performed regularly as a soloist, and with his elder brothers Acchan and Lacchu Maharaj. He moved to Delhi in 1955 and taught Kathak at the Shriram Bharatiya Kala Kendra, establishing the tradition of the Lucknow Gharana in Delhi. He was very famous for his abhinaya and bhav batana, and he performed such in the court style of sitting and enacting. He taught his nephew, the famous Birju Maharaj and many other famous Kathak dancers of India. He is survived by his sons Ram Mohan and Kishan Mohan who are also accomplished dancers, and gurus. He was the recipient of the Padma Shri in 1958 and Sangeet Natak Academy Award in 1967.",
              "artists_images": [
                "/downloaded_images/20b938edf4b337abe41ea5a1ab94604e.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/aea3a1fd3cadbaefe4d07fedaec24a37.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/f78e02787a0bf986f44c7dcd9f0a5953.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/08d781af700028b5d00ffd1cbd9ff305.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/504a29fe517a31bf6d9b81eb296e8de8.webp",
                "/downloaded_images/30b0ad6e77aa7e0b89961f5f6819dead.webp"
              ],
              "single_gestures": "",
              "single_gestures_images": [],
              "joint_gestures": "",
