              "id": "13d10398",
              "name": "Nongkrem",
              "desc": "Costume - Women wear traditional costumes while men are often adorned with vibrant colours holding swords and white yak hair whisk.\nPurpose - Celebrated during autumn to please the powerful Goddess for plentiful harvest and prosperity of people.\nPerformers - Both men and women.\nAccompainments - Accompanied by traditional music including the drum and wind instrument tangmuri.\n (Ref: NCERT Textbook fekr1, Ch. 15)",
