    {
      "id": "mizoram",
      "name": "Mizoram",
      "geography": {
        "capital": "Aizawl",
        "key_cities": []
      },
      "facts": [
        "**Weaving**: is an integral part of the Mizo culture and the women learn how to weave at an early age. Puans in numerous designs are produced by them on traditional looms. These are somewhat like lungis worn by the women, and are their native dress. Puans are noted for their beautiful design and intricate embroidery which is invariably worked out along with the weave. Mizos have a wealth of motifs. Mizo women also make attractive shawls and shoulder bags. The Hmars weave many designs and some of the important ones are thangsuo puon meaning famous cloth, puon laisen meaning cloth with red in the middle, hmarm - the loin cloth worn by women and zakuolaisen - the blouse piece used mainly by the unmarried girls."
      ],
      "art_forms": {
        "paintings": [
          {
            "id": "af03c8f3",
            "title": "Bamboo & reed craft art",
            "name": "Bamboo & reed craft art",
            "desc": "Bamboo & reed craft art",
