        "handicrafts": [
          {
            "id": "cezy2hyao",
            "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Stone inlay work work",
            "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Stone inlay work work",
            "desc": "Pietra dura is Agra's fabled inlay work of precious stones like lapiz lazuli and machelite on marble. The mosaics formed by the inlay work range from beautiful floral patterns to free flowing flower and vine themes on table tops, bowls, wall hangings, etc. The best of pietra dura work featuring delicate and intricate mosaics in jewel like colours is made in Agra. Vrindavan is a centre of exquisite alabaster figures, fret work traceries and jaals.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/stone-inlay-agra.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "pay15trsk",
            "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Embroidery",
            "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Embroidery",
            "desc": "Lucknow's craftswomen are known for their Chikankari. The name \u0091chikan\u0092 seems to have been derived from the Persian word, either Chikan, Chikin or Chikeen. It means a kind of cloth wrought with needle\u0096work. A delicate and subtle embroidery, reminiscent of the shadow work of Isphahan in Persia, Chikankari's charm lies in the minuteness, evenness and sheer excellence of craft as well as the use of white embroidery on white cloth. Chief among the stitches are murree, lepchi, keelkangan, bakhia in which forms are outlined on the right side with minute stitches while the threads are concentrated on the wrong side, giving the motifs an opaque shadowy quality. The motifs of chikankari range from floral and vine themes to birds, animals and arabesques.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/Chikankari-1.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "gmiqspumh",
            "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Weaving",
            "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Weaving",
            "desc": "Sari weaving is a cottage industry for millions of people around Varanasi. Most of the silk for the Banarasi saris comes from south India, mainly from Bangalore. Kinkhab is the art of using gold and silver thread on fine silk and cotton to create the rich brocades of Varanasi gold thread on a silver background creates the beautiful shimmering tissues. Breathtakingly beautiful, they are embellished with bird, animal and geometric patterns in the butidar and jaal style.Weavers known as karigars weave saris in workshops known as karkhanas. The design motifs of these brocades are intricate floral and foliage patterns, kalga and bel, and in sari pallaus and dupattas a string of upright leaves called jhalar.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/banarasi-saree3.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "slo6pmsz7",
            "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Carpet Weaving",
            "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Carpet Weaving",
            "desc": "Varanasi and its neighboring areas are well known for carpet making. The Varanasi-Bhadohi-Mirzapur belt in Uttar Pradesh produces maximum number of carpets in the country. They have their own distinct designs such as the Taj Mahal, Kethariwala Jal, Jamabaz, Kandhari, etc. Embossed, sculpted carpets in the Chinese style are also produced in Mirzapur.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/carpet-mirzapur.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "925yyoz0g",
            "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Metal craft",
            "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Metal craft",
            "desc": "Moradabad in western Uttar Pradesh produces large quantities of metalware, specially brassware and it is famous for its coloured enamelling and intricate engraving. While engravings of the nakashi type are done on tinned surface, khudai is done on lac coated unpolished brass on which a pointed steel pencil is used to make the design later filled with lac of different hues. Today, apart from traditional vases, stools, etc. beautiful contemporary bowls, trays, and images of different deities are being made in Moradabad.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/brass-surahi.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "c5hdnjhnj",
            "title": "Woodwork",
            "name": "Woodwork",
            "desc": "Saharanpur is well-known for its carved and brass inlay furniture items and other artifacts. Sheesham, sal and dudhi wood are used to make well-finished screens, room dividers and furniture items featuring jaali or lattice work and brass inlay work in floral and geometric patterns. The furniture artifacts are attractive with an increasing amount of contemporary design input.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/wood-saharanpur.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "ycyr313cs",
            "title": "Pottery",
            "name": "Pottery",
            "desc": "Khurja pottery has evolved a style of its own by raising the pattern with the use of thick slips into a light relief. The shades of the pottery are in warm autumnal colours like orange, brown, and a special light red. Floral designs in sky blue are worked against a white background. A speciality of Khurja is a type of long pitcher decorated in relief by a thick slip. Specialized glazed items like tableware for modern use are produced in Chinhat and Mausalia. A very special kind of earthenware peculiar to Nizamabada and Azamgarh districts of Uttar Pradesh is distinguished by its dark lustrous finish.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/khurja.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "tx66tq6b0",
            "title": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Glass",
            "name": "Uttar Pradesh- Handicrafts- Glass",
            "desc": "Ferozabad is a glass town where the entire community seems to be involved in making glassware. Originally only glass bangles were made here, but now all types of sophisticated glassware including tasteful tableware is produced.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttar_Pradesh/firozabad-bangles.webp",
            "historical_significance": "",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "a75c876d",
            "title": "Chikankari embroidery",
            "name": "Chikankari embroidery",
            "desc": "Chikankari embroidery",
            "img": ""
          },
