      "art_forms": {
        "paintings": [
          {
            "id": "uptuj6cm4",
            "title": "painting",
            "name": "painting",
            "desc": "The art of Miniature painting flourished in Garhwal under the influence of Mughal and Western Pahari schools, and that too without any feudal patronage. The arts and crafts of Uttarkhand, of which an amazingly rich variety exists today, demand and indeed deserve a closer look. A rich",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttarkhand/miniature_painting.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "4eavw39lu",
            "title": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Painting -Aipana",
            "name": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Painting -Aipana",
            "desc": "The rural art of Kumaon known as aipana, a local adaptation of alpana, (plaster with fingers) is practiced by the women folk. The other sacred and dainty paintings of this region are the pitha, the seat of Siva worshipped on auspicious days and decorated with geometrical patterns and chowki (seat) of Lakshmi and Saraswati using floral and traditional patterns.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttarkhand/aipan.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "hy3ikcg4u",
            "title": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Wall Painting",
            "name": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Wall Painting",
            "desc": "In the Kumaon region, the usual wall paintings are known as the bar-boond (dash and dot). The pattern is made first by making a number of dots to outline the design and then joining those dots by lines of different colours. Each pattern is known by the number of dots used. For example in the pattern called masti-bar-mat, a composition of ten dots and the colours yellow, red, violet and green are used. The designs are mostly floral and very lively.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttarkhand/bar-boond.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
            "id": "vkfz9tj47",
            "title": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Painting",
            "name": "Uttarakhand- Handicrafts- Painting",
            "desc": "Kumaon is also famous for pattas, special pictures made on festival days depicting the particular deity connected with the festival as also the deity's various aspects that are worshipped on the occasion.",
            "img": "/state-images/Uttarkhand/pattas.webp",
            "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
            "materials": ""
          },
          {
