      ],
      "fairs_and_festivals": [
        {
          "id": "wtijfry43",
          "title": "Uttarakhand- Fairs & Festivals",
          "name": "Uttarakhand- Fairs & Festivals",
          "desc": "Numerous fairs and festivals are celebrated all over Uttarkhand every year. In the Kumaon hills, the festivals celebrated are Uttarayani Mela, Shravan Mela, Gananath Mela and Dwarahat Mela. The Uttarayani Mela is held at a number of places including Bageshwar, Rameshwar, Salt Mahadev, Chitrashila (Ranibagh), Pancheshwar, etc. on fourteenth of January of every year. Two large fairs are held at Jageshwar, one on the occasion of Shivratri (February) and the other in the month of Shravan (July-August). A dip on the occasion in the Jat Ganga and Brahmakund, near the temple complex, is of great religious significance. Gananath is 47 km from Almora. A fair is held here every year on Kartik Poornima (October \u0096 November), when thousands of pilgrims come to worship Lord Shiva and Ganesh. Nanda Devi Mela are held at Almora, Nainital, Nauti, Dandidhara, Munsyari and Ranikhet, of which the Almora and Roopkund fairs are the most famous. At Almora, thousands of people take part in a procession carrying the dola of Nanda Devi. The Nanda Devi temple of Almora is the venue for the three day long Nanda Devi Fair. Of great religious and cultural significance, it is held at Nanda Devi Temple in memory of Goddesses Nanda and Sunanda. It is said to have started in Kumaon during the reign of Raja Kalyan Chand in the sixteenth Century. Nestled in the lap of nature Almora is one of the most beautiful places in Kumaon region. Just besides the city flows the Koshi (Kaushaki) and Suyal (Salmali) rivers. In the ninth century Almora was ruled by Katyur dynasty. By 16th century this place was ruled by Chandravanshi rulers. This town was established by King Balo Kalyan Chand in 1563. This place was the capital city of the Kumaon region. The forts, monuments and palaces evidence of the splendour this place had in the past.",
          "img": "/state-images/Uttarkhand/uttarayanmela.webp",
          "historical_significance": "Contemporary",
          "materials": ""
        }
      ],
