    {
      "id": "ad012de7",
      "name": "Kuchipudi",
      "desc": "Kuchipudi, from Andhra Pradesh and Telangana, derives its name from the village of Kuchipudi, which remains home to several traditional dance families. It follows a rich dance-drama tradition and is distinctive for its integration of vachika abhinaya (spoken word) along with an expressive dance. Often theatrical in nature, it includes elements of acting; and at times, dancers perform intricate sequences on a brass plate, showcasing remarkable balance and skill. \n\nThe basic stance is similar to Bharatanatyam\u2019s aramandi, but is less deep. The dance is distinctive for its quickfootedness, hip movements, leaps, sculpturesque poses and speed. The dancers wear silk fabrics stitched for easy movement, with a special drape called gochi kattu. They also wear traditional temple jewellery.",
      "img": "/downloaded_images/8be2a30e9b792d82b160a1265353ebe7.webp",
      "images": [
        "/downloaded_images/8be2a30e9b792d82b160a1265353ebe7.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/7ac6ca76d62b22bfd6cca9d59a1f7cf5.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/3977e58fadddf70888f5fdd0ceaae1d3.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/9d0d5488114e210e7533b1b9eff295b0.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/c2f518374128814276b29267576b5026.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/8338248d169519f21e8a0f2fad1f6081.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/66604688a74fae4247daaf0f4d9aae04.webp"
      ],
      "artists": "1.Vempati Chinna Satyam - \nHe has been largely responsible for the revival of Kuchipudi dance in post-independent India. Padma Bhushan by Govt. of India, \"Fellow\" by Sangeet Natak Akademi (New Delhi) in 1991, Kalidas Samman by Government of Madhya Pradesh in 1992, Kalaimamani by Govt. of Tamil Nadu in 1994. \n\n2. Vedantam Satyanarayana Sarma \n \nHe is a legend of Kuchipudi dance, was admired, acknowledged, revered as one of the best when it came to portrayal of female impersonation roles.\n\nHe was the first recipient of the Sangeet Natak Akademi award for a Kuchipudi artiste in 1961. He got his Fellowship of the Sangeet Natak Akademi in 1967, followed by Padma Shri in 1970. He was also conferred the Kalidas Sammam award in 1988.",
      "artists_images": [
        "/downloaded_images/9d141515da9e4a33c260aef0bf0054eb.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/dc1f41f5112264ae1ad14b8ecdda4b7b.webp",
        "/downloaded_images/ede55150cd3de7891a6864a32c82716b.webp",
