      "artists": "DK Pattammal\nShe was an eminent Carnatic vocalist who was born in 1919. She also used music to spread the message of patriotism during India\u2019s freedom struggle. She sang many patriotic songs in several films. She was invited to sing in All India Radio on August 15, 1947, to commemorate India\u2019s independence.\nShe was also the first woman to sing Ragam Thanam Pallavi, a complex form of music, on stage. (Ref: NCERT Textbook eebu1, Ch. 14)",
